Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patch 0001.
Engram disk offload for unified-memory boxes (GB10): table rows are read from the checkpoint's safetensors shards at
lookup time (pread pool in engram_disk.cpp, enqueued as a host node on the lookup stream) into pinned staging that the
upstream lookup kernel reads through UVA, instead of ~100 GB of pinned host tables per rank at TP=2.
Oct 8: the eager-only event guard between the inline and prefetch streams is skipped under CUDA graph capture (a wait on
an event recorded outside the capture invalidated FULL_DECODE_ONLY capture; each captured forward joins the prefetch
stream before reading its rows).

